open_issues:
No real-hardware acceptance (spec 4.6). Not verified on a device:
- surprise removal of an open handle (does MIM_CLOSE arrive? does a stale handle still answer?);
- how long WinMM's list lags after a Plug and Play arrival (R2);
- Windows MIDI Services multi-client mode and port naming.
The only real input, the DDJ-FLX10, was deliberately never opened (exclusive access, rekordbox running).

Test thresholds differ from the spec's Linux numbers because this machine's load starves the GTK thread (measured idle-loop gaps of 203-472 ms):
- the 100 ms main-loop-gap and page-build assertions became deterministic checks that no WinMM listing or open ever runs on the GTK thread (values are still printed);
- LOST via the notification or MIM_CLOSE must come within 0.9 s while dead handles keep answering, so the list check cannot be the cause;
- a UI reconnect must come within 1.9 s, before the next 5 s retry;
- LOST via the list check within 3 s; PORT with a 600 ms list lag between 0.55 and 1.6 s.
One single-process run hit the old 1.2 s reconnect bound at 1261 ms (traced: environmental, the mechanism takes about 17-63 ms).
